-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 2 (b): ss 18 to 19, change of
-- employer, transfer of employment, and the offence.
--
-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore
-- Statutes Online (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  Every
-- `-- src:` line copies a line of that file (script-generated); every quotation in
-- a FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment is a phrase of it (checked by a script).
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its
-- own words.  NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts and is never to
-- be read as no.  "marginal (a)" or "marginal (b)" marks the branches that rest on
-- one of the two readings for a lawyer (NOTES.md).

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 2 Contracts of service, ss 18 to 19`

§§ `s 18 Change of employer`

-- src:1037 | 18.—(1) If by or under any written law a contract of employment
-- src:1038 | between any body corporate and an employee is modified and some
-- src:1039 | other body corporate is substituted as the employer, the employee’s
-- src:1040 | period of employment at the time when the modification takes effect
-- src:1041 | counts as a period of employment with that other body corporate, and
-- src:1042 | the change of employer does not break the continuity of the period of
-- src:1043 | employment.
@ref s 18(1) (src:1037-1043)
GIVEN `a contract of employment between a body corporate and an employee is modified by or under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `some other body corporate is substituted as the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(1) the employee's period of employment counts as a period of employment with the other body corporate` MEANS
    IF `a contract of employment between a body corporate and an employee is modified by or under a written law` AND `some other body corporate is substituted as the employer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If by or under any written law a contract of employment between any body corporate and an employee is modified and some other body corporate is substituted as the employer" -- ruled 2026-11-05: an unmet "if"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 18(1) (src:1037-1043)
GIVEN `a contract of employment between a body corporate and an employee is modified by or under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `some other body corporate is substituted as the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(1) the change of employer breaks the continuity of the period of employment` MEANS
    IF `a contract of employment between a body corporate and an employee is modified by or under a written law` AND `some other body corporate is substituted as the employer`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the change of employer does not break the continuity of the period of employment" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks only of a modification by or under a written law and the substitution of another body corporate
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1045 | (2) If on an employer’s death the employee is taken into the
-- src:1046 | employment of the personal representatives or trustees of the
-- src:1047 | deceased, the employee’s period of employment at the time of the
-- src:1048 | death counts as a period of employment with the employer’s personal
-- src:1049 | representatives or trustees, and the death of the employer does not
-- src:1050 | break the continuity of the period of employment.
@ref s 18(2) (src:1045-1050)
GIVEN `the employer has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is taken into the employment of the personal representatives or trustees of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(2) the employee's period of employment counts as a period of employment with the employer's personal representatives or trustees` MEANS
    IF `the employer has died` AND `the employee is taken into the employment of the personal representatives or trustees of the deceased`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an employer’s death the employee is taken into the employment of the personal representatives or trustees of the deceased" -- ruled 2026-11-05: an unmet "if"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 18(2) (src:1045-1050)
GIVEN `the employer has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is taken into the employment of the personal representatives or trustees of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(2) the death of the employer breaks the continuity of the period of employment` MEANS
    IF `the employer has died` AND `the employee is taken into the employment of the personal representatives or trustees of the deceased`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the death of the employer does not break the continuity of the period of employment" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) speaks only of an employee taken into the employment of the personal representatives or trustees
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1052 | (3) If there is a change in the partners, personal representatives or
-- src:1053 | trustees who employ any person, the employee’s period of
-- src:1054 | employment at the time of the change counts as a period of
-- src:1055 | employment with the partners, personal representatives or trustees
-- src:1056 | after the change, and the change does not break the continuity of the
-- src:1057 | period of employment.
@ref s 18(3) (src:1052-1057)
GIVEN `there is a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees who employ the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(3) the employee's period of employment counts as a period of employment with the partners, personal representatives or trustees after the change` MEANS
    IF `there is a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees who employ the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If there is a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees who employ any person" -- ruled 2026-11-05: an unmet "if"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 18(3) (src:1052-1057)
GIVEN `there is a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees who employ the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(3) the change breaks the continuity of the period of employment` MEANS
    IF `there is a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees who employ the person`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the change does not break the continuity of the period of employment" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) speaks only of a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees who employ any person
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 18A Transfer of employment`

-- src:1061 | 18A.—(1) If an undertaking (whether or not it is an undertaking
-- src:1062 | established by or under any written law) or part thereof is transferred
-- src:1063 | from one person to another —
-- src:1065 | (a) such transfer does not operate to terminate the contract of
-- src:1066 | service of any person employed by the transferor in the
-- src:1067 | undertaking or part transferred but such contract of service
-- src:1068 | has effect after the transfer as if originally made between
-- src:1069 | the person so employed and the transferee; and
@ref s 18A(1)(a) (src:1061-1069)
GIVEN `an undertaking or part of it is transferred from one person to another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(1)(a) the transfer operates to terminate the contract of service of the person employed` MEANS
    IF `an undertaking or part of it is transferred from one person to another` AND `the person was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such transfer does not operate to terminate the contract of service of any person employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an undertaking ... or part thereof is transferred from one person to another"
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 18A(1)(a) (src:1061-1069)
GIVEN `an undertaking or part of it is transferred from one person to another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(1)(a) the contract of service has effect after the transfer as if originally made between the person employed and the transferee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an undertaking ... or part thereof is transferred from one person to another" -- ruled 2026-11-05: an unmet "if"
        IF NOT `an undertaking or part of it is transferred from one person to another` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the person was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred" (scope limit with no "only", ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1071 | (b) the period of employment of an employee in the
-- src:1072 | undertaking or part transferred at the time of transfer
-- src:1073 | counts as a period of employment with the transferee, and
-- src:1074 | the transfer does not break the continuity of the period of
-- src:1075 | employment.
@ref s 18A(1)(b) (src:1071-1075)
GIVEN `an undertaking or part of it is transferred from one person to another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(1)(b) the period of employment of the employee counts as a period of employment with the transferee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an undertaking ... or part thereof is transferred from one person to another" -- ruled 2026-11-05: an unmet "if"
        IF NOT `an undertaking or part of it is transferred from one person to another` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the person was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an employee in the undertaking or part transferred at the time of transfer" (scope limit with no "only", ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 18A(1)(b) (src:1071-1075)
GIVEN `an undertaking or part of it is transferred from one person to another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(1)(b) the transfer breaks the continuity of the period of employment` MEANS
    IF `an undertaking or part of it is transferred from one person to another` AND `the person was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the transfer does not break the continuity of the period of employment" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an undertaking ... or part thereof is transferred from one person to another"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1080 | (2) Without affecting subsection (1), on completion of a transfer
-- src:1081 | referred to in that subsection —
