GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(2)(b) the act or omission is deemed to have been done by the transferee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on completion of a transfer referred to in that subsection" -- "on completion of" read as "upon", and "upon" as "where" (assumed, not ruled: fork F-EVENT); ruled 2026-11-05 (b)
        IF NOT `the transfer referred to in subsection (1) is completed` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the act or omission was done before the transfer by the transferor in respect of the contract of service` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any act or omission done before the transfer by the transferor in respect of that contract of service" (scope limit with no "only", ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
