DECLARE `s 18A(8) Matter of a dispute` IS ONE OF
    `s 18A(8)(b)(i) a dispute from a collective agreement entered into between the transferor and the trade union while the collective agreement remains in force`
    `s 18A(8)(b)(ii) a dispute from the transfer of the employee's employment from the transferor to the transferee`
    `s 18A(8) a dispute from some other matter`

-- src:1151 | (8) Where, immediately before a transfer referred to in
-- src:1152 | subsection (1), a trade union is recognised by the transferor for the
-- src:1153 | purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 in respect of any
-- src:1154 | employee who in consequence of the transfer becomes the employee
-- src:1155 | of the transferee, the trade union, after the transfer —
-- src:1157 | (a) is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the
-- src:1158 | purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 if, after the
-- src:1159 | transfer, the majority of employees employed by the
-- src:1160 | transferee are members of the trade union; or
-- src:1162 | (b) in any other case, is deemed to be recognised by the
-- src:1163 | transferee only for the purpose of representing the
-- src:1164 | employee on any dispute arising —
-- src:1166 | (i) from any collective agreement that was entered into
-- src:1167 | between the transferor and the trade union while the
-- src:1168 | collective agreement remains in force; or
-- src:1173 | (ii) from the transfer of the employee’s employment
-- src:1174 | from the transferor to the transferee under this
-- src:1175 | section.
@ref s 18A(8) (src:1151-1175)
GIVEN `the trade union was recognised by the transferor for the purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 in respect of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in consequence of the transfer the employee becomes the employee of the transferee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the majority of employees employed by the transferee are members of the trade union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(8)(a) the trade union is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, immediately before a transfer referred to in subsection (1), a trade union is recognised by the transferor ... in respect of any employee who in consequence of the transfer becomes the employee of the transferee" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" not met
        IF NOT (`the trade union was recognised by the transferor for the purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 in respect of the employee` AND `in consequence of the transfer the employee becomes the employee of the transferee`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the majority of employees employed by the transferee are members of the trade union` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any other case, is deemed to be recognised by the transferee only for the purpose of representing the employee on any dispute" -- marginal (a)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 18A(8)(b) (src:1162-1175)
GIVEN `the trade union was recognised by the transferor for the purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 in respect of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in consequence of the transfer the employee becomes the employee of the transferee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the majority of employees employed by the transferee are members of the trade union` IS A BOOLEAN
      dispute IS A `s 18A(8) Matter of a dispute`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(8)(b) the trade union is deemed to be recognised by the transferee for the purpose of representing the employee on the dispute` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, immediately before a transfer referred to in subsection (1), a trade union is recognised by the transferor ... in respect of any employee who in consequence of the transfer becomes the employee of the transferee" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" not met
        IF NOT (`the trade union was recognised by the transferor for the purposes of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 in respect of the employee` AND `in consequence of the transfer the employee becomes the employee of the transferee`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (b) is "in any other case", and where the majority are members paragraph (a) applies and does not speak of the disputes of paragraph (b)
        IF `the majority of employees employed by the transferee are members of the trade union` THEN NOTHING
        IF (dispute EQUALS `s 18A(8)(b)(i) a dispute from a collective agreement entered into between the transferor and the trade union while the collective agreement remains in force`) OR (dispute EQUALS `s 18A(8)(b)(ii) a dispute from the transfer of the employee's employment from the transferor to the transferee`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "deemed to be recognised by the transferee only for the purpose of representing the employee on any dispute arising" -- marginal (a)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "for a period of 18 months after the date of the transfer or until the date of its
-- expiry as specified in the collective agreement, whichever is the later".  The Act
-- (and the Interpretation Act 1965, staged in DEPENDENCIES, which defines "month" and
-- gives no rule for counting months) does not say how to count 18 months after a day;
-- the corresponding day of the month 18 months on is taken (NOTES.md, fork F-18A(8A)).
-- src:1177 | (8A) For the purposes of subsection (8)(b), any collective
-- src:1178 | agreement that was entered into between the transferor and the
-- src:1179 | trade union of the affected employees and in force immediately
-- src:1180 | before the transfer continues in force between the transferee and the
-- src:1181 | trade union of the affected employees for a period of 18 months after
-- src:1182 | the date of the transfer or until the date of its expiry as specified in the
-- src:1183 | collective agreement, whichever is the later.
@ref s 18A(8A) (src:1177-1183)
GIVEN `the day of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `the date of expiry specified in the collective agreement` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 18A(8A) the last day on which the collective agreement continues in force between the transferee and the trade union` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date of expiry specified in the collective agreement`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `eighteen months after the day of the transfer`
    WHEN JUST expiry THEN
        IF `eighteen months after the day of the transfer` LESS THAN expiry THEN expiry ELSE `eighteen months after the day of the transfer`
    WHERE
        `eighteen months after the day of the transfer` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY `the day of the transfer`) ((DATE_MONTH `the day of the transfer`) PLUS 18) (DATE_YEAR `the day of the transfer`)

-- src:1187 | (9) A dispute or disagreement between the transferor and an
-- src:1188 | employee or the transferee and an employee arising from a transfer
-- src:1189 | under subsection (1), whether before or after the transfer, may be
-- src:1190 | referred by a party to the dispute or disagreement to the
-- src:1191 | Commissioner under section 115 and is deemed to be a dispute to
-- src:1192 | which that section applies.
@ref s 18A(9) (src:1187-1192)
GIVEN `the dispute or disagreement is between the transferor and an employee, or the transferee and an employee, and arises from a transfer under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(9) a party may refer the dispute to the Commissioner under section 115, and it is deemed to be a dispute to which that section applies` MEANS
    IF `the dispute or disagreement is between the transferor and an employee, or the transferee and an employee, and arises from a transfer under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A dispute or disagreement between the transferor and an employee or the transferee and an employee arising from a transfer under subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1194 | (10) Where a dispute or disagreement has been referred to the
-- src:1195 | Commissioner pursuant to subsection (9), the Commissioner has, in
-- src:1196 | addition to the powers conferred under section 115, the powers —
-- src:1198 | (a) to delay or prohibit the transfer of employment of the
-- src:1199 | employee to the dispute from the transferor to the
-- src:1200 | transferee under subsection (1); and
@ref s 18A(10)(a) (src:1194-1200)
GIVEN `the dispute or disagreement has been referred to the Commissioner pursuant to subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(10)(a) the Commissioner has the power to delay or prohibit the transfer of employment of the employee` MEANS
    IF `the dispute or disagreement has been referred to the Commissioner pursuant to subsection (9)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a dispute or disagreement has been referred to the Commissioner pursuant to subsection (9)" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" not met
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1202 | (b) to order that the transfer of employment of the employee to
-- src:1203 | the dispute from the transferor to the transferee under
-- src:1204 | subsection (1) be subject to any terms that the
-- src:1205 | Commissioner considers just.
@ref s 18A(10)(b) (src:1202-1205)
GIVEN `the dispute or disagreement has been referred to the Commissioner pursuant to subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(10)(b) the Commissioner has the power to order that the transfer of employment be subject to terms that the Commissioner considers just` MEANS
    IF `the dispute or disagreement has been referred to the Commissioner pursuant to subsection (9)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a dispute or disagreement has been referred to the Commissioner pursuant to subsection (9)" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" not met
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1228 | (12) Nothing in this section prevents a transferee of an undertaking
-- src:1229 | referred to in subsection (1) and an employee whose contract of
-- src:1230 | service is preserved under that subsection or a trade union
-- src:1231 | representing such an employee from negotiating for and agreeing
-- src:1232 | to terms of service different from those contained in the contract of
-- src:1233 | service that is preserved under that subsection.
@ref s 18A(12) (src:1228-1233)
GIVEN `the parties are the transferee and an employee whose contract of service is preserved under subsection (1), or the transferee and a trade union representing such an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(12) the parties may negotiate for and agree to terms of service different from those of the preserved contract of service` MEANS
    IF `the parties are the transferee and an employee whose contract of service is preserved under subsection (1), or the transferee and a trade union representing such an employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in this section prevents a transferee ... and an employee whose contract of service is preserved under that subsection or a trade union representing such an employee"
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 18A(13) Kind of change of hands` IS ONE OF
    `s 18A(13) the disposition of a business as a going concern`
    `s 18A(13) a transfer effected by sale`
    `s 18A(13) a transfer effected by amalgamation`
    `s 18A(13) a transfer effected by merger`
    `s 18A(13) a transfer effected by reconstruction`
    `s 18A(13) a transfer effected by operation of law`
    `s 18A(13) some other change of hands`

DECLARE `s 18A(13) Kind of undertaking` IS ONE OF
    `s 18A(13) a trade`
    `s 18A(13) a business`
    `s 18A(13) something else`

-- src:1237 | “affected employee” means any employee of the transferor who
-- src:1238 | may be affected by a transfer under subsection (1) or may be
-- src:1239 | affected by the measures taken in connection with such a
-- src:1240 | transfer;
@ref s 18A(13) "affected employee" (src:1237-1240)
GIVEN `the person is an employee of the transferor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee may be affected by a transfer under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee may be affected by the measures taken in connection with such a transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(13) "affected employee" the employee is one` MEANS
    IF `the person is an employee of the transferor` AND (`the employee may be affected by a transfer under subsection (1)` OR `the employee may be affected by the measures taken in connection with such a transfer`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“affected employee” means any employee of the transferor who may be affected by a transfer under subsection (1) or may be affected by the measures taken in connection with such a transfer"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1242 | “trade union” means a trade union which has been —
-- src:1244 | (a) registered under any written law for the time being in
-- src:1245 | force relating to the registration of trade unions; and
-- src:1247 | (b) accorded recognition by the employer pursuant to
-- src:1248 | section 17(1) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960;
@ref s 18A(13) "trade union" (src:1242-1248)
GIVEN `the trade union has been registered under any written law for the time being in force relating to the registration of trade unions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trade union has been accorded recognition by the employer pursuant to section 17(1) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(13) "trade union" the trade union is one` MEANS
    IF `the trade union has been registered under any written law for the time being in force relating to the registration of trade unions` AND `the trade union has been accorded recognition by the employer pursuant to section 17(1) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“trade union” means a trade union which has been"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1250 | “transfer” includes the disposition of a business as a going
-- src:1251 | concern and a transfer effected by sale, amalgamation,
-- src:1252 | merger, reconstruction or operation of law;
@ref s 18A(13) "transfer" (src:1250-1252)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 18A(13) Kind of change of hands`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(13) "transfer" the change of hands is a transfer` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 18A(13) some other change of hands` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“transfer” includes the disposition of a business as a going concern and a transfer effected by sale, amalgamation, merger, reconstruction or operation of law" opens the class
        NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1254 | “undertaking” includes any trade or business.
@ref s 18A(13) "undertaking" (src:1254-1254)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 18A(13) Kind of undertaking`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(13) "undertaking" the thing is one` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 18A(13) something else` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“undertaking” includes any trade or business" opens the class
        NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 19 Offence`

-- No penalty is stated in section 19: the penalty "for which no penalty is otherwise
-- provided" is in section 112 (ea2); its answer is taken as an input (seam S15, and
-- SEAMS-FOUND.md: S15 names only s 48).
-- src:1258 | 19. Any employer who enters into a contract of service or collective
-- src:1259 | agreement contrary to the provisions of this Part shall be guilty of an
-- src:1260 | offence.
@ref s 19 (src:1258-1260)
GIVEN `the employer enters into a contract of service or collective agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is contrary to the provisions of Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19 the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the employer enters into a contract of service or collective agreement` AND `it is contrary to the provisions of Part 2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any employer who enters into a contract of service or collective agreement contrary to the provisions of this Part"
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 19 (src:1258-1260)
GIVEN `the answer of s 112 first conviction` IS A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
      `the answer of s 112 subsequent conviction` IS A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
      `the employer has been convicted of an offence before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
`s 19 the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 19 states no penalty, and the penalty "for which no penalty is otherwise provided" is in section 112
    IF `the employer has been convicted of an offence before` THEN `the answer of s 112 subsequent conviction` ELSE `the answer of s 112 first conviction`
